  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "Yes. Even though the amount is small and the person is a longtime friend, reporting is the right course if they have committed refund fraud or violated company policy. Your professional duty and the integrity of the organization outweigh personal ties. Small incidents can become a pattern and failing to act can expose you to liability or accusations of favoritism. Recommended approach: check and follow company policy, document the facts, consider a private nonaccusatory conversation with your friend or give them a chance to correct the mistake if policy permits, and if not (or if they refuse), report the incident to the appropriate supervisor/HR channel while maintaining confidentiality and avoiding personal retaliation."
}

